       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under supervision. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day). This is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily. The \"1600\" may have been meant as a daily total.\n\nIf you really do want 1,600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale. I would still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
