       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. The dose is also well past the point where a clinical rationale would make it safe. At 6,400 mg/day, the expected harm (GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, cardiovascular events) is high, and ibuprofen has no established benefit above 3,200 mg/day. Taking this dose at face value could seriously hurt the patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** I can enter 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day) right now. I can add a note that escalation was requested by a specialist.\n- **Get pharmacy and the specialist involved.** A pharmacist can review the request. If the specialist documents the rationale and the prescriber enters it directly with pharmacy sign-off, it can go through the hospital's high-dose override process.\n- **Consider alternatives.** If standard ibuprofen dosing failed, another NSAID, an adjunct, or a different drug class may fit better. The specialist could advise.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 800 mg four times daily order?"
      }
     ],
